-- title:
--   Two-cusp integrality of (⟨ e⟩ f)∣₂ W
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime and $M$ a nonzero natural number with $p \mid M$ but $p^2 \nmid M$, and let $H$ be a subgroup of $(\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times$ containing every unit $u$ whose image under the reduction map `ZMod.unitsMap` associated with $(M/p) \mid M$ is $1$; thus $H$ contains the kernel of $(\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/(M/p))^\times$. Let $W$ be an Atkin–Lehner datum for $(M,p)$, that is, data $R$, $a$, $b$ with $M = pR$ and $pa - Rb = 1$, and let $e \in (\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times$. Let $f$ be a weight-two cusp form for the congruence subgroup $\Gamma_H(M) \le \mathrm{SL}(2,\mathbb{Z})$ (the image in $\Gamma_0(M)$ of the preimage of $H$ under the lower-right-entry character `gamma0Units`), and assume $f$ lies in [`CuspForm.twoCuspIntegralSet M H 2 p ⊥`](def/CuspForm_TwoCuspLattice.html#L54): for every operator $t$ in the subring `heckeRingH M H 2` of $\mathbb{C}$-linear endomorphisms generated by the Hecke generators, every Atkin–Lehner datum $W'$ for $(M,p)$ and every $n$, the $n$-th coefficient of the $q$-expansion (of width $1$) of $t f$ and that of $\mathrm{alSlash}\,W'\,2\,(t f) = (t f)\mid_2 W'$ both lie in the bottom subring $\bot$ of $\mathbb{C}$, i.e. are rational integers. Let $g$ be a weight-two cusp form for $\Gamma_H(M)$ whose underlying function equals $(\langle e \rangle f)\mid_2 W$, where $\langle e\rangle =$ [`CuspForm.diamondLinH 2 e`](def/CuspForm_HeckeOperatorFormsGammaH.html#L132). Then $g$ also lies in [`CuspForm.twoCuspIntegralSet M H 2 p ⊥`](def/CuspForm_TwoCuspLattice.html#L54).
--
--   This is the statement that the lattice of two-cusp integral weight-two forms on $\Gamma_H(M)$ is stable under the Atkin–Lehner involution at $p$ composed with a diamond operator. It is used in the construction of the reduction maps to polar and regular differentials on the modular curve, in particular by [`CuspForm.exists_infReductionMap_and_wReductionMap_range_le_ssPolarDifferentials`](thm.html#CuspForm.exists_infReductionMap_and_wReductionMap_range_le_ssPolarDifferentials) and [`ModularCurve.coe_map_mem_regularDifferentials_of_atkinLehnerPinAlong`](thm.html#ModularCurve.coe_map_mem_regularDifferentials_of_atkinLehnerPinAlong), and it cites the saturation criterion [`CuspForm.mem_twoCuspIntegralSet_of_forall_qCoeff_diamondLinH_mem`](thm.html#CuspForm.mem_twoCuspIntegralSet_of_forall_qCoeff_diamondLinH_mem) together with the commutation of diamond and Atkin–Lehner operators and the weight-two identity $W \circ W' = \langle \delta \rangle$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_CuspForm_mem_twoCuspIntegralSet_of_coe_eq_alSlash_diamondLinH.lean

